   "stem": {
      "text": "The graph of the polar curve \\( r = 3 - 2 \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\) for \\( 1.7 \\le \\theta \\le 3.35 \\) is shown. Using a calculator, find the value of \\( \\theta \\) that corresponds to the point on the curve farthest from the x-axis. Justify your answer, show the setup, and give the value correct to three decimal places.",
      "setup_required": true,
      "command_verb": "find"
   },
   "answer_key": {
      "form": "numeric",
      "mathjson": 2.010189688456593,
      "decimals": 3
   },
   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "The distance from the x-axis is \\( |y| \\), where \\( y = r\\sin\\theta = \\left(3 - 2 \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}\\right) \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\).",
         "point_type_id": "BC-PT-99005",
         "rule_named": "polar to rectangular conversion"
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "Set \\( \\frac{dy}{d\\theta} = \\left(3 - 2 \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}\\right) \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 2 \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} = 0 \\). On the interval a calculator gives one solution, \\( \\theta \\approx 2.010 \\).",
         "mathjson": 2.010189688456593,
         "point_type_id": "BC-PT-99013",
         "rule_named": "critical angle"
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "Compare the candidates, the critical angle and both endpoints: \\( |y(1.7)| \\approx 3.231 \\), \\( |y(2.010)| \\approx 3.485 \\), \\( |y(3.35)| \\approx 1.026 \\). The largest distance is at \\( \\theta \\approx 2.010 \\), so that is the farthest point.",
         "point_type_id": "BC-PT-99011",
         "rule_named": "candidates test"
      }
   ],
